## 🧩 Project Structure

```
src/
├── app/
│   ├── (auth)/                      → Public pages (login, signup)
│   ├── (dashboard)/                → Protected routes
│   └── layout.tsx                  → Root layout
├── components/
│   ├── atoms/                      → Stateless UI (Input, Button)
│   ├── molecules/                  → Combos like Label + Input + Error
│   └── layout/                     → Global reusable layouts (e.g., AuthLayout)
├── features/
│   ├── auth/                       → Feature-specific logic
│   │   ├── components/             → Atomic structure: atoms, molecules, organisms
│   │   ├── layout/                 → Feature layout if needed only
│   │   ├── context/                → Local context for auth
│   │   ├── hooks/                  → `useLogin`, `useSignup` (React Query based)
│   │   ├── services/               → Business logic layer (validates, transforms, handles DTO)
│   │   ├── api/                    → API calls using Axios
│   │   ├── repository/             → Optional repo layer for data abstraction
│   │   └── model/                  → Types/interfaces for request/response
│   └── dashboard/                  → Similar setup for another domain
├── contexts/                       → Global context providers (Auth, Theme, Toast)
├── dto/                            → Shared DTOs (LoginRequest, SignupRequest, etc.)
├── hooks/                          → Global reusable hooks (e.g., useDebounce, useClickOutside)
├── constants/                      → Shared constants (colors, regex, form messages)
├── routes/                         → Route mapping constants (e.g., `ROUTES.LOGIN`)
├── styles/
│   └── globals.css                 → Contains `@theme` variables (Tailwind CSS v3+)
├── utils/                          → Pure utility functions (e.g., validation, formatting)
├── types/                          → Shared app-wide types/interfaces
├── data/                           → Optional: static data, dropdowns, locales, etc.
public/
└── assets/
    └── logo/
        └── basobas-logo.png        → Branding image


