✅ Additional Key Implementation Rules
Ensure Responsive Design Across All Devices

All components must be fully responsive and mobile-first using Tailwind utility classes.

Layouts and forms should gracefully adapt from mobile → tablet → desktop.

Support Both Light and Dark Themes

Use Tailwind’s dark: class strategy.

Respect system preferences and dynamically adapt using ThemeContext.

Use color variables defined in @theme (e.g., bg-[var(--color-primary)]) to maintain consistency across themes.

Optimize Render Performance and User Experience

Use useCallback, useMemo, and React.memo() appropriately to prevent unnecessary re-renders.

Add smooth, meaningful animations using Tailwind’s transition, duration, and ease classes (e.g., form shake on error, button press animation).

Keep state localized where necessary; avoid prop-drilling.


## 💡 Summary

| Layer               | Rules & Notes |
|---------------------|---------------|
| Atoms/Molecules     | Stateless, reusable, no hooks or context |
| Organisms           | Can contain basic state/logic, but not heavy logic |
| Templates (Optional)| Pure structure/layout, no logic |
| Features            | Self-contained: api, services, hooks, context, components |
| Global Context      | Theme, Auth, Toast → in `contexts/` |
| Global Hooks        | Shared utilities → `hooks/` |
| React Query Flow    | api → services → hook → used in page only |
| Tailwind CSS        | Use `@theme` in globals.css only |
| Commenting Standard | Every function must have doc-comment |

